@simonklee I reproduced what `v2` does after this failure by injecting the reported `Failed to create TextBuffer` error. The tested fix is on [`tui-allocation-v2`](https://github.com/peterkc-io/opencode/tree/tui-allocation-v2) at `20f2619`.

The [earlier comment](https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode/issues/35053#issuecomment-5192847629) compares `dev` and `v2`, explains the proposed fix, and lists the test results.

If this approach looks right, I can open a focused PR against `v2`.

**Update (2026-08-06):** Both halves of this feature have now landed upstream — the remaining gap is a small wiring change in the built-in DeepSeek profile.

**1. DeepSeek officially shipped native web search (Jul 31, 2026)**
DeepSeek's official announcement (X/@deepseek_ai + changelog) for the V4-Flash official release confirms native web search support. The Anthropic-compatible endpoint (`https://api.deepseek.com/anthropic`) accepts `server_tool_use` blocks and returns `web_search_tool_result` — exactly the protocol path this issue asked for.

**2. OpenCode's runtime now handles provider-defined tools**
Since the V2 runner rework, provider-hosted tools pass through untouched: tool-calls with `providerExecuted: true` skip local dispatch (see "Provider-defined / hosted tools" in `packages/llm/AGENTS.md`). `packages/llm/src/protocols/anthropic-messages.ts` accepts `web_search` as a provider-defined tool and encodes results back as `server_tool_use` + `web_search_tool_result` blocks.

**3. What's still missing: the built-in DeepSeek profile is registered as OpenAI-compatible**
`packages/llm/src/providers/openai-compatible-profile.ts` still maps deepseek → `https://api.deepseek.com/v1` (Chat Completions), and models.dev lists no `tools` capability for DeepSeek models. So out of the box, `/connect deepseek` still cannot expose `web_search`.

**Immediate workaround (works today):** register DeepSeek as a custom Anthropic-protocol provider:

```jsonc
// opencode.json
{
  "provider": {
    "deepseek-anthropic": {
      "npm": "@ai-sdk/anthropic",
      "options": { "baseURL": "https://api.deepseek.com/anthropic" },
      "models": {
        "deepseek-v4-flash": { "name": "DeepSeek V4 Flash" }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

The Anthropic route lowers a declared `web_search` tool to `server_tool_use` and DeepSeek executes it server-side.

**Ask:** can the built-in DeepSeek profile be switched to the Anthropic protocol (or models.dev updated to mark DeepSeek with `web_search` tools)? DeepSeek's own integration docs already recommend opencode >= v1.14.24 for their Anthropic-compatible API, so this looks like a small change that closes the issue.
